From 9efefea6fceb335eb52f8b5d2086fa94e10d64d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 02:08:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 087/100] sunxi: h713: name the HY310 backlight channel - PWM2
 at 25 kHz (Q8)

The note at the deinit's "two deliberate omissions" called the backlight
channel unresolved and quoted channel 0 from display_cfg.xml against
channel 5 from panel_config.ini, concluding that our PWM2-on-PB4 dimmer
matched neither.

AP3d section 7.2 read PanelControl::getPWMConfig@0x1CE30 and the six
[PWMSetting] words it hands to Thal_Vp_SetBacklightPwmInfo: for the HY310
they are channel 2, polarity 1, freq 25000, vs_lock 1, min 1, max 100.
Channel 2 at 25 kHz is PWM2, the channel we drive. The channel 5 belongs
to board B's ini - line 425 of this file has said so all along - and
display_cfg.xml's channel 0 at 1.2 MHz is the firmware default that the
vendor ARM overwrites with those six words.

Comment only, no code change. What stays open is the polarity (ini 1,
stock runtime DTB panel_pwm_pol 0, we follow the DTB) and the measured
fact in docs/dead-ends.md that stepping PWM2's duty moved no light on two
boards - which is why the deinit still leaves the channel alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c
index ce7a0652e32..293f9771cb3 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c
@@ -7145,10 +7145,16 @@ static void h713_disp_sample(void)
  *
  * Two deliberate omissions:
  *
- *   - The backlight is not touched. Which PWM drives it is still unresolved:
- *     display_cfg.xml says channel 0, panel_config.ini says channel 5, and the
- *     dimmer we implemented drives PWM2 on PB4, which matches neither. Turning
- *     off the wrong channel would be theatre.
+ *   - The backlight is not touched. Which channel drives it is settled now:
+ *     the HY310's panel_config.ini asks for PWM channel 2 at 25 kHz, exactly
+ *     the PWM2-on-PB4 dimmer we built. The channel 5 this note used to quote
+ *     is board B's ini, as line 425 already says, and display_cfg.xml's
+ *     channel 0 at 1.2 MHz is the firmware's own default, which the vendor
+ *     ARM overrides with the six [PWMSetting] words (AP3d 7.2). What is still
+ *     open is the polarity -- the ini says 1, the stock runtime DTB's
+ *     panel_pwm_pol says 0, and we follow the DTB -- and the measurement in
+ *     docs/dead-ends.md, where stepping PWM2's duty moved no light on two
+ *     boards. Switching a channel off that never moved light buys nothing.
  *
  *   - The display PLLs and mod clocks are left running. Disabling a block's
  *     clock while something still reaches for it is the documented way to wedge
